+### Level meter in a Player layout (`ui.player_layout_meter`)
+
+An XML Now Playing layout can show a stereo level meter (a VU meter) by
+naming widgets: `lv_bar` for a straight meter, `lv_arc` for a round dial,
+and any object as a needle. The player finds them and moves them; no Lua runs
+per frame, and nothing is measured while no layout with a meter is on screen.
+
+| Name | Shows |
+| --- | --- |
+| `vu_left`, `vu_right` | The level of each channel, with VU-like ballistics: quick up, slower down. An `lv_bar` or an `lv_arc`. |
+| `vu_peak_left`, `vu_peak_right` | The peak of each channel, held for a moment and then falling. An `lv_bar` or an `lv_arc`. |
+| `vu_needle_left`, `vu_needle_right` | Any object, turned about its transform pivot with the level: 45 degrees left of upright when empty, 45 degrees right when full. |
+| `vu_band_1` … `vu_band_10` | A spectrum: the level of the mono mix in ten bands an octave apart, centred on 31, 62, 125, 250, 500 Hz, 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16 kHz. An `lv_bar` or an `lv_arc` each; name only the bands you show. |
+| `vu_band_peak_1` … `vu_band_peak_10` | A cap that rides each band's bar, held for a moment and then falling. With `mode="range"` it is drawn as a short mark. |
+| `vu_meter` | Optional `lv_obj` around the meter. The group, captions included, is hidden with the transport controls while the lyrics are open; without it only the bars are. |
+
+```xml
+<lv_obj name="vu_meter" x="0" y="520" width="#screen_w" height="38" scrollable="false" style_bg_opa="0" style_border_width="0" style_pad_all="0" clickable="false">
+    <lv_label name="caption_vu_left" text="L" x="30" y="2" width="18" height="content" style_text_font="font_16" />
+    <lv_bar name="vu_left" x="56" y="8" width="394" height="8" style_radius="4" />
+    <lv_bar name="vu_peak_left" mode="range" x="56" y="8" width="394" height="8" style_radius="4" style_bg_opa="0" />
+    <lv_label name="caption_vu_right" text="R" x="30" y="24" width="18" height="content" style_text_font="font_16" />
+    <lv_bar name="vu_right" x="56" y="30" width="394" height="8" style_radius="4" />
+    <lv_bar name="vu_peak_right" mode="range" x="56" y="30" width="394" height="8" style_radius="4" style_bg_opa="0" />
+</lv_obj>
+```
+
+A round dial is an arc from 225 to 315 degrees with a needle pivoted at the
+arc's centre, which is the fan the needle sweeps:
+
+```xml
+<lv_arc name="vu_left" x="-28" y="8" width="260" height="260" bg_start_angle="225" bg_end_angle="315" style_arc_width="6" style_arc_width:indicator="6" style_arc_rounded="true" style_bg_opa="0" style_pad_all="0" />
+<lv_arc name="vu_peak_left" x="-28" y="8" width="260" height="260" bg_start_angle="225" bg_end_angle="315" style_arc_width="6" style_arc_width:indicator="6" style_arc_opa="0" style_bg_opa="0" style_pad_all="0" />
+<lv_obj name="vu_needle_left" x="101" y="26" width="3" height="112" style_radius="3" style_bg_color="0xffffff" style_bg_opa="255" style_transform_pivot_x="1" style_transform_pivot_y="112" style_border_width="0" style_pad_all="0" />
+```
+
+- A peak arc is always drawn as a short mark on the dial. An arc's knob is
+  hidden. Any `bg_start_angle`/`bg_end_angle` works for the arcs; the
+  needle's swing is fixed at 45 degrees either side of upright.
+- A layout with needles should use the `vu_meter` group, since a needle is
+  not hidden on its own while the lyrics are open.
+A spectrum is a row of vertical bars, each with its cap laid over it:
+
+```xml
+<lv_bar name="vu_band_1" x="17" y="14" width="26" height="122" orientation="vertical" style_radius="4" style_bg_opa="38" />
+<lv_bar name="vu_band_peak_1" mode="range" x="17" y="14" width="26" height="122" orientation="vertical" style_radius="4" style_bg_opa="0" />
+```
+
+- The spectrum's scale runs from -54 dB to full scale in each band. It is
+  only measured while a layout that names a band is on screen; it costs
+  noticeably more processor time than the level alone.
+- All of these are optional and independent. The player sets each bar's
+  range and value; `min_value`, `max_value` and `value` in the XML are ignored.
+- The scale is linear in decibels, from -48 dB at the empty end to full scale
+  at the other. The level is RMS, read so that a full-scale sine fills the bar.
+- A peak bar with `mode="range"` is drawn as a short mark at the held peak
+  instead of a filled bar. Put it over the level bar with a transparent track
+  (`style_bg_opa="0"`), as above, for a peak-hold mark.
+- The indicator takes the theme accent and a level bar's or arc's track the
+  same rail color as the seek bar. Local XML style properties outrank both; use a part
+  selector for the indicator, for example `style_bg_color:indicator="0xffffff"`.
+- A vertical meter is a bar taller than wide, or `orientation="vertical"`.
+- The bars are not clickable, so swipes pass through them.
+- The meter follows what is heard, allowing for the output buffer. Over
+  Bluetooth and a USB DAC that allowance is an estimate. Native DSD (DoP)
+  output has no PCM level to read and leaves the meter empty.
+- Check `plugin.has_capability("ui.player_layout_meter")` before offering a
+  layout built around the meter: an older player shows the bars empty.
+
 ### `plugin.refresh_theme()`
 
 Applies icon changes and the Home and launcher layouts, without disturbing
